AB  - Novice programmers who use large language model (LLM) assistants alternate between productive struggle and unproductive stalling, yet instructors rarely see which is which. We instrumented an introductory programming course (N=212) with editor and assistant telemetry and asked teaching assistants to label 1,904 thirty-second windows as productive struggle, stalling, help-seeking, or off-task.
