N1  - <div data-schema-version="9"><h1>Ostrowski et al. 2025 (L@S) - notes</h1><p><span class="citation" data-citation="%7B%22citationItems%22%3A%5B%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2Flocal%2FmyLibrary%2Fitems%2FQQR79WDT%22%5D%7D%5D%7D">(<span class="citation-item">Ostrowski et al., 2025</span>)</span> closest prior work to TutorTrace. MUST cite in related work + discussion.</p><ul><li>N=212 CS1, 1,904 windows, 4 states (productive struggle / stalling / help-seeking / off-task). ours has stalled-after-error as its own state, they fold it into stalling</li><li>their kappa 0.64 (4 TAs, 10% overlap). ours 0.71 across 3 raters -&gt; say this carefully, different schemes</li><li>strongest stalling signal = near-identical repeated prompts (edit distance &lt; 15%). we see the same thing in VizPI replays, worth one sentence</li><li>they report a leakage check (0.58 when same-student windows removed). note to self: double check our own split before submission</li><li>discussion: flags as prompts for a human check-in, not auto interventions. aligns w our framing</li></ul><p>heads up: arXiv v1 (2507.01842v1) has 0.69 F1 / kappa 0.62, camera-ready has 0.71 / 0.64. cite the camera-ready numbers. I have both pdfs floating around (Downloads + Desktop/papers), the zotero one is camera-ready</p></div>
