N1  - <div data-schema-version="9"><p><span class="citation" data-citation="%7B%22citationItems%22%3A%5B%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2Flocal%2FmyLibrary%2Fitems%2FMVTX3YSV%22%5D%7D%5D%7D">(<span class="citation-item">Nakamura and Feld, 2025</span>)</span> cite this for why 30s windows. kappa 0.66 at 30s vs 0.48 at 10s vs 0.61 at 60s.</p><ul><li>tinkering vs stuck = 44% of their disagreements. our guide v3 &quot;stalled-after-error&quot; rule does basically what their decision rule does (no successful run + reverts) -&gt; mention</li><li>they let raters flag mixed windows (11%). we forced one label. reviewer might ask. prep a line for limitations</li></ul></div>
