AB  - When a course permits an AI assistant, instructors still want to know how much of a submission a student wrote. We study paste events in an instrumented editor used by 296 CS1 students alongside an integrated assistant. A classifier using paste size, time since the last assistant response and token overlap with that response identified assistant-originated pastes with F1 = 0.88 against assistant logs. Across the term, 23% of final submissions contained more than half pasted assistant code, concentrated in the last 24 hours before deadlines. We discuss uses of provenance signals that support learning rather than policing.
