TI  - What Will Students Share? Consent and Comfort with Fine-Grained Telemetry in Educational IDEs
AU  - Brennan, Colm
AU  - Zhou, Wei
AU  - Adler, Ruth
T2  - arXiv preprint
M3  - arXiv:2602.11873
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026/06/13/
AB  - Research on novice programming increasingly depends on fine-grained telemetry, yet little is known about what students are willing to share. We surveyed 418 students at three universities about eight data streams, from submission history to webcam video, and four uses, from aggregate research to individual instructor review. Comfort was high for submissions (89%) and keystrokes (61%) but low for assistant prompts (38%), which students saw as revealing confusion. Restricting use to aggregate dashboards raised comfort by 22 percentage points on average. We propose a consent design that separates streams and uses.
