AB  - Classifiers of learner behavioral states are almost always trained and evaluated within a single course. We trained a gradient-boosted classifier on labeled windows from a Python CS1 course and evaluated it on two other courses: a Java data structures course and a block-based CS0 course. Macro-F1 fell from 0.72 in-course to 0.61 and 0.55. Per-course normalization of rate features recovered part of the gap (0.66 on data structures). Errors concentrated on the "stuck" state, whose behavioral signature depended on the language's error messages. We recommend reporting cross-course results as a standard check.
